WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.634
-Oh, you're a stud.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:05.868
-I just was watching you
Thanksgiving at the parade.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:06.934
Awesome job.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.901
-Oh, yeah. Thank you.
Roots, yeah.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.267
-It was super cool.
-Thank you, bud.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.267
We had a good time.
How was your Thanksgiving?

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.200
-It was really nice.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.534
We were making dinner

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:15.868
while we were watching you.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.601
Well, it was actually lunch
this year, which was --

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.567
-Yeah.
-Yeah, it's good when it's lunch

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.334
because that means that my wife
isn't gonna go into the bedroom

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.133
and put her pajamas on
and then come out

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.834
to try to get people
out of the house, but...

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:28.067
-[ Laughs ]
-Because it ends early.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.334
-It ends early,
and everyone goes home.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:30.400
You go, "Thank you so much."
-But you know what?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.734
I'll tell you what --
There's a guy --

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.634
I wrote his name down because
it's hard to remember.

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:35.534
His name is J. Kenji López-Alt.

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.934
Do you know who this is?
-No.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:40.267
-This is the guy that saved
our Thanksgiving this year,

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:44.167
or let's say
changed it forever for the good.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.968
Every year, we talk about
the turkey thing --

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:50.334
how we're going to do it,
wet brine, dry brine.

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.834
-Yes. Spatchcock.
-Spatchcock.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.000
-Spatchcock, new thing.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.667
Everyone is spatchcocking.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.701
-This guy is a spatchcocker.

00:00:57.701 --> 00:00:59.734
This guy
is an avid spatchcocker.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:03.701
[ Laughter ]
We didn't actually -- What?

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:04.901
-That's on his resume.
-What's funny?

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.367
-He's an avid spatchcocker.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:10.033
-We didn't actually spatchcock
this year.

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:12.868
But what we did was

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.434
before it goes into the oven,

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.701
you cover it in mayonnaise.

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.167
[ Audience groans, laughs ]

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:20.467
You love mayonnaise,
right, Jimmy?

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:21.400
Jimmy?

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.367
What's up? What's up?

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:27.634
You haven't lived
until you've taken a raw bird

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.701
and filled every single crevice

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:32.567
with herbed mayonnaise.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.767
I'm not kidding.
-Oh, my God. Herbed mayonnaise?

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:35.834
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.667
-That makes it
even grosser sounding.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.300
Herbed mayonnaise?

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.200
Was it room temperature
herbed mayonnaise?

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.634
-Yeah, room temperature.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:46.033
It was the breast tur--
It was the best turkey

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.200
that we've ever had.
-Yeah. Right.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.667
-And the experience --
-Yeah, right,

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.200
it was the best turkey
you've ever had.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.634
-I'm telling you.
-Give me a break.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.200
What was this man's name again?

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.601
-J. Kenji López-Alt.
-Yeah. No thanks.

00:01:56.601 --> 00:02:00.300
-No. And rubbing it
in the crevices, it's kind of --

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.801
-Do you tell everyone
you did that?

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:03.267
-Yeah. I mean,
it's kind of like --

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.901
-People try to trick me because
they know I don't like mayo.

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.534
And they go,
"Why don't you have this corn?"

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.100
-No, they told me --
-"Try, it Jimmy."

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.067
I go, "I know you rolled it
in mayonnaise.

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.067
I'm not gonna eat it.
Don't trick me into doing it."

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.334
-You're good at a lot of things.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:14.968
You don't need to be
a great mayonnaise lover

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.934
on top of everything else.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:18.167
You know? Don't feel bad.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.801
-But what did it do to it?
Did it tenderize it?

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.434
Did it make it tangy?
Did you get a zip?

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:25.000
-I feel like it's like the Upper
West Side version of manliness.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.734
I felt like I was --
-Really? On top of the world?

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:29.767
-It was like I was rubbing it
in these crevices.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.167
It felt like I was
naked bow hunting or something.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:33.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:35.334
-In the middle of the woods
somewhere, just running?

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:38.167
-I don't know, but it was
absolutely delicious.

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:40.734
You don't taste the mayonnaise.
It's crispy.

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:42.868
-But then why do it
if you don't taste it?

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.534
If you don't taste it,
get it out of the house.

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:46.100
-All right. You can --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.334
You can talk to J. Kenji
López-Alt about this.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.734
-I want to talk to him about it.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.367
-He's a scientist,

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:52.634
and it has to do
with the proteins

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:54.701
interacting with the skin
of the bird.

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:55.968
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah, I'm serious.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.667
-Just spatchcock it, man.
That's what you got to do.

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:58.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:01.367
-Just spatchcock that thing.
-Just spatchcock it.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.801
-Hey, we have a lot
to talk about.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.434
-Okay.
-Last time you were here,

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.601
you told me
that you were about to do

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.868
"Beverly Hills Cop 4"
with Eddie Murphy.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.067
-I did.
-You did?

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.634
-I did it, yeah.
-How was it?

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:13.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-So fun. So fun.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.934
-I'm so psyched.
I love Eddie.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.267
And I love Kevin Bacon.
-Eddie was great.

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.934
I mean, he made me laugh
so many times.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.067
And, you know, he said to me --
It was really sweet

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.601
'cause, you know,
you're working with somebody,

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.567
and he's such a big
giant iconic star,

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.367
and, you know, for me, too,
you know?

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.801
I mean, it's like --
It's not like

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:32.234
I'm just, you know,
"Oh, whatever. That's cool.

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:33.767
It's Eddie Murphy."
I mean, it's Eddie Murphy.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:34.834
You know?
-Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:37.667
-And he's like,
"Yeah, we're '80s guys."

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:41.133
And I think what he meant was
that our movies or big movies

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:43.701
kind of came out in the '80s --
at least my big movies.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:44.734
He kept having him.

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:47.100
That was my one shot.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.234
So, but it was great.

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:51.300
We had a good time.
-Had you met him before?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.868
-No, I had never met him before.

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:55.834
But he told me
some great stories.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.467
-Can you tell anyone
who you're playing?

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.234
-I can tell you --

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:02.033
I think I can say I'm playing
a Beverly Hills cop.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:04.567
-Wow. All right, that's --

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.167
-I think that's all I can say.
-No spoilers.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:07.467
-But you know what I did?

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:11.434
I binge-watched all three
of them before to get ready.

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:14.367
And I get this thing where,
like, songs get into my head.

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:15.467
So, for months, it was --

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:21.567
[ Humming "Beverly Hills Cop"
theme ]

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:22.767
Find that key.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:28.601
[ Both vocalize
"Beverly Hills Cop" theme ]

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:33.000
♪♪

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.234
-Oh, nice.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:37.634
♪♪

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:38.701
All right.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:40.767
♪♪

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.067
[ Laughs ] Wow.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.400
♪♪

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.801
-Yeah, but now you got it
in all of our heads.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.067
Why would you do this?

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.167
-I mean, it's --
-Is it trapped in your head?

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:50.133
-Well, it is now.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:51.601
-Axel F.
-It's back.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:53.334
-Axel F. was his name.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.267
Yeah, that was Axel Foley.
Yeah, that was his --

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.901
-This is actually called
"Beverly Hills Cop: Axel Foley."

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.100
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.434
-Oh, my go-- So you're doing
that giant thing.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:04.067
And then you do "Guardians of
the Galaxy: Holiday Special."

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:05.901
-I know, man.
-It's very funny.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:08.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.267
It's on Disney Plus.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:10.801
[ French accent ]
It's on Disney Plus.

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.067
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:13.267
-[ Normal ] I don't want to
give too much away

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:15.000
for people who haven't seen
the special yet.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.367
But in this holiday special,

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:20.834
it's a call-back to the first
"Guardians of the Galaxy" movie

00:05:20.834 --> 00:05:23.801
'cause Chris Pratt's character
is obsessed with you.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:25.834
-Yes.
He thinks I'm a great hero.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:27.033
[ Laughs ]

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.501
-Yeah. So, they --

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:31.501
I don't want to --
but they kidnap you, kind of.

00:05:31.501 --> 00:05:35.133
-They do, yeah.
Yeah, they kidnap me.

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:36.400
-I saw a tweet, by the way.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.934
A fan tweeted this,
and I thought this was very fun.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.968
From TheAlphaVictor.
It said...

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.234
That's how excited fans are
that this happened.

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:48.300
And you made it happen.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.200
I love that you did this.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.567
-I had so much fun, you know?

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:53.267
When I was probably
starting out --

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:56.300
when I had amazing experiences,
I kind of used to feel like

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.934
I was too cool
to react to things, you know?

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.868
I would be like,
"Yeah, whatever, Meryl Streep.

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:03.901
Okay. Whatever, yeah, going to
the moon, okay, whatever."

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:05.033
You know what I mean?

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:06.467
But I'm at a point
in my life now

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:09.133
where I can just stop and go,
"Oh, my God.

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:11.567
This is crazy,
what I do for a living.

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:12.934
This is so cool."

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:15.367
When I walked onto the set
of "Guardians of the Galaxy"

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:19.200
and saw all of those aliens,
not to mention the Guardians,

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.968
and they're all in different
make-ups and wardrobe,

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:25.100
and there's Christmas stuff
all over the place.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.267
I literally was like --
one of those moments like,

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:28.501
"Damn, this is fun."

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:29.868
-That's exactly
what I'm talking about.

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:32.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes! It's supposed to be fun.

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:33.400
This is all fun.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.734
-I am so grateful
to have this gig.

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:37.234
-I couldn't happen
to a cooler dude.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:38.634
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:40.868
Here's Kevin Bacon in "Guardians
of the Galaxy: Holiday Special."

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:42.067
Take a look at this.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:43.834
-Oh!
-911, can I help you?

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:46.400
Hello?

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.868
-There's two --
I don't know what they are --

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:49.100
people in costumes.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:50.234
Aah!

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.934
-♪ I want an alien
for Christmas ♪

00:06:52.934 --> 00:06:56.334
♪ Bring me an alien
this year ♪

00:06:56.334 --> 00:06:59.601
♪ I want a little green guy
about three feet high ♪

00:06:59.601 --> 00:07:02.868
♪ With 17 eyes
who knows how to fly ♪

00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:08.033
♪ I want an alien
for Christmas this year ♪

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:10.801
♪♪

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:13.634
-Aah! Aah! Aaaaah!

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:15.234
[ Groans ]

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.133
Oh!

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:18.968
[ Breathing heavily ]

00:07:18.968 --> 00:07:25.100
♪♪

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.367
-Come on.
You're the best.

00:07:26.367 --> 00:07:28.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.567
Only you can do
all this cool stuff.

00:07:29.567 --> 00:07:31.634
I love it.
-It was fun.

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.267
-What I also think
is cool about it --

00:07:33.267 --> 00:07:35.467
Also, in this, by the way,
on the soundtrack here,

00:07:35.467 --> 00:07:39.767
you get to sing a holiday song
with the great band, Old 97's.

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:42.033
It is on the soundtrack,
which I have here.

00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:43.501
But this is very exciting.

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.734
Not only are you awesome,
but you came here tonight.

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:48.067
You're going to perform
with Old 97's

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:51.234
the song from "The Guardians of
the Galaxy: Holiday Special"

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:53.167
called "Here it is,
Christmastime"

00:07:53.167 --> 00:07:54.434
on the show tonight.

00:07:54.434 --> 00:07:56.033
Kevin Bacon, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:56.033 --> 00:07:58.534
"Guardians of the Galaxy:
Holiday Special," streaming now

00:07:58.534 --> 00:07:59.934
on Disney Plus.

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:02.067
Kevin is performing
after the break.

00:08:02.067 --> 00:08:03.133
Stick around!

